  "preview": "The Wall Street Journal (WSJ), commonly known as the Journal, is an American newspaper based in Midtown Manhattan, New York City. It provides extensive coverage of news, especially business and finance, and operates on a subscription model that requires readers to pay for access to most articles and other content. The Journal is published six days a week by Dow Jones & Company, a division of News Corp.\nAs of 2025, The Wall Street Journal is the largest newspaper in the United States by print circulation, with about 412,000 print subscribers. It has more than four million digital subscribers, the second-most in the nation after The New York Times. The newspaper is one of the United States' newspapers of record. The first issue of the newspaper was published on July 8, 1889. The editorial page of the Journal is typically center-right in its positions, while its news reporting is more centrist. The newspaper has won 39 Pulitzer Prizes.\n\n== History ==\n\n=== Founding and 19th century ===",
  "topic": "technology",
  "text": "The Wall Street Journal (WSJ), commonly known as the Journal, is an American newspaper based in Midtown Manhattan, New York City. It provides extensive coverage of news, especially business and finance, and operates on a subscription model that requires readers to pay for access to most articles and other content. The Journal is published six days a week by Dow Jones & Company, a division of News Corp.\nAs of 2025, The Wall Street Journal is the largest newspaper in the United States by print circulation, with about 412,000 print subscribers. It has more than four million digital subscribers, the second-most in the nation after The New York Times. The newspaper is one of the United States' newspapers of record. The first issue of the newspaper was published on July 8, 1889. The editorial page of the Journal is typically center-right in its positions, while its news reporting is more centrist. The newspaper has won 39 Pulitzer Prizes.\n\n== History ==\n\n=== Founding and 19th century ===",
